WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.584 --> 00:00:04.129
Hey, everyone, we're here
for our last Wine Down...

00:00:04.212 --> 00:00:05.755
-Whoo!
-PRENTICE PENNY: of the season.

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:08.174
Eight of these things,
can you believe it? Oh, my God.

00:00:08.258 --> 00:00:11.344
I'm joined once again by Issa's
ride-or-die, Molly,

00:00:11.428 --> 00:00:12.846
the actress Yvonne Orji.

00:00:12.929 --> 00:00:13.847
-ISSA RAE: Whoo!
-Hello, guys.

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:15.473
This was an eventful season,

00:00:15.557 --> 00:00:17.100
and we are so excited
to get into it.

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:19.978
This episode has Issa
going forth professionally,

00:00:20.228 --> 00:00:22.230
and feeling comfortable
with her friends even

00:00:22.313 --> 00:00:23.940
as she faces down 30.

00:00:26.276 --> 00:00:28.361
-Y'all, Nathan came back.
-Where he been at?

00:00:28.445 --> 00:00:30.196
-He ghosted.
-I dunno, V, you sent him away.

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:32.282
-So like, what was up with that?
-Yeah. 'Cause he's--

00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:35.118
'Cause he had no right--
Girl, it's your 30th birthday.

00:00:35.493 --> 00:00:37.829
Why you-- Why you like,
"Can we talk about this dude

00:00:37.912 --> 00:00:39.789
like he's a real dude?"
Girl, it was your 30th!

00:00:39.956 --> 00:00:41.166
And I was just lookin' out
for you.

00:00:41.583 --> 00:00:43.918
When you're not calling
or texting for a whole month,

00:00:44.002 --> 00:00:45.253
get outta here, no.
You don't care about me.

00:00:45.336 --> 00:00:47.130
I don't care what's going on
in your life. Do better.

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:48.548
But it was rooted
in other things.

00:00:48.631 --> 00:00:51.176
Like, Molly was bringing her own
baggage into Issa's thing.

00:00:51.259 --> 00:00:53.470
-Lemme be real. Real--
-(LAUGHTER)

00:00:53.762 --> 00:00:55.305
I just gave her a look like...

00:00:55.513 --> 00:00:58.433
Real me appreciates
Molly's gesture.

00:00:58.516 --> 00:00:59.559
-Okay.
-ISSA: But,

00:00:59.642 --> 00:01:01.895
Issa was spun out
over this dude.

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:03.563
She's at a point
where she's like,

00:01:03.646 --> 00:01:05.106
"I wanna make decisions
for myself,

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:06.149
and I wanna have clarity."

00:01:06.483 --> 00:01:08.985
And it felt like Molly
was bringing her own issues--

00:01:09.068 --> 00:01:10.653
But it was a bad decision,
like--

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:12.155
-What was a bad decision?
-YVONNE ORJI: Here's the thing.

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:14.282
I feel like Molly's like,
"Girl, you deserve the best."

00:01:14.365 --> 00:01:17.035
Like, Molly thinks the world
of Issa, she thinks that like,

00:01:17.118 --> 00:01:20.246
if we're gonna be adults,
we should be the same way like,

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:21.456
Dro was trash, like,

00:01:21.539 --> 00:01:23.041
"Oh, you just gon' have a baby
with Candice?"

00:01:23.124 --> 00:01:25.043
But you didn't even give him
a chance to explain.

00:01:25.126 --> 00:01:27.754
It doesn't matter!
There's a whole child comin'.

00:01:27.837 --> 00:01:28.838
I think Molly too, sometimes,

00:01:29.214 --> 00:01:32.217
especially given what she said
in episode seven about like,

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:33.718
"Dudes are gonna say
whatever they--"

00:01:33.802 --> 00:01:35.094
You don't need to hear
his explanation!

00:01:35.512 --> 00:01:36.930
-PRENTICE: That's true.
-YVONNE: You don't have to hear
whatever he says,

00:01:37.013 --> 00:01:38.598
'cause he's gonna say
whatever's gonna sound right,

00:01:38.681 --> 00:01:41.142
to make a whole month
of disappearing sound amazing.

00:01:41.226 --> 00:01:42.310
-Right.
-Or normal.

00:01:42.519 --> 00:01:43.937
And girls fall for it
all the time,

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:45.480
and I think that's where Molly's
coming from.

00:01:45.563 --> 00:01:47.315
-So, it reads as negative...
-I love...

00:01:48.107 --> 00:01:49.567
-You go girl.
-Well no, I love that Molly

00:01:49.651 --> 00:01:52.237
does not ride for Daniel,
she does not ride for Nathan,

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:53.363
but she fucks with Lawrence.

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:54.864
I think Molly's okay

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:56.491
with Lawrence not being
in the picture,

00:01:56.574 --> 00:02:00.495
that's why she was like, "Oh!
We-- We good? How do we feel?"

00:02:00.703 --> 00:02:04.040
But I think she's not okay
with Nathan being a replacement.

00:02:04.332 --> 00:02:06.918
So, the one thing that we
always talked about in the room,

00:02:07.001 --> 00:02:09.629
we wanted to say like Molly,
after three years,

00:02:09.712 --> 00:02:12.006
like we wanted to kinda put
Molly into a relationship,

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:15.260
or at least a... like,
the blossoming of something

00:02:15.343 --> 00:02:17.303
that could be like,
"Oh, could this work?"

00:02:17.387 --> 00:02:19.889
And we went in the room a lot of
times about, should he be white?

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:21.307
Should he be this?
Should he be that?

00:02:21.391 --> 00:02:23.226
What would this be if he
was Asian like,

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:24.769
like what does that do
for a character?

00:02:24.853 --> 00:02:26.354
Kinda like, take her out
of her comfort zone.

00:02:26.437 --> 00:02:27.981
'Cause I think with Molly,
we've always tried to like,

00:02:28.231 --> 00:02:30.024
-challenge her way of thinking.
Right? Like...
-Yes.

00:02:30.108 --> 00:02:32.569
Okay, if it's not a fairy tale,
is that okay? Okay, if it's not,

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:34.153
does it have to be this sort
of like, you know,

00:02:34.237 --> 00:02:35.488
I'm in an open relationship
type of thing.

00:02:35.572 --> 00:02:37.031
-Yeah.
-This idea of Andrew came up,

00:02:37.115 --> 00:02:39.075
and we really were sort of like,
we really want to make sure

00:02:39.158 --> 00:02:42.161
that we don't just make Molly
be this sort of tragic... woman

00:02:42.245 --> 00:02:43.830
-Shakespearean flaw.
-who can't be in a relationship.

00:02:43.913 --> 00:02:46.666
But that was a real thing for us
and we wanted to sort of like,

00:02:46.749 --> 00:02:48.918
okay, but if it is gonna be
a guy who's not black,

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:50.837
-YVONNE: Mm-hmm.
-how do we explore that? And I--

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:52.672
In a way that hasn't been
explored before.

00:02:52.755 --> 00:02:55.091
And I think Alexander,
the guy who plays Andrew,

00:02:55.174 --> 00:02:56.509
he's great in so many ways.

00:02:56.593 --> 00:02:57.635
-And I think Molly--
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:58.052 --> 00:03:00.638
Molly's that chick who might
need somebody when she's like,

00:03:00.722 --> 00:03:01.639
"Hey, yeah!" To be like,

00:03:01.723 --> 00:03:02.765
"You need a hug?
Don't make me hug you."

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:03.808
-You know? Like, she's...
-Right.

00:03:03.892 --> 00:03:05.768
She's that chick that like needs

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:07.478
the reverse of whatever
she's dishing.

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:10.189
The finale in a way,
just listening to it is like,

00:03:10.273 --> 00:03:12.567
oh, there's a lot of people
getting answers, right?

00:03:12.817 --> 00:03:14.652
Like, Andrew's kinda getting
some answers

00:03:14.736 --> 00:03:15.862
about where Molly is,

00:03:15.945 --> 00:03:18.531
Issa's getting some answers
about where Nathan is.

00:03:18.615 --> 00:03:20.158
And even Lawrence is sorta
getting some answers

00:03:20.241 --> 00:03:23.119
about where either Issa is
and his stuff with Condola, so,

00:03:23.202 --> 00:03:24.871
I think it's really interesting
that everybody's sorta getting

00:03:24.954 --> 00:03:25.997
a chance to like say,

00:03:26.289 --> 00:03:28.791
"Here's what the situations are.
Now, what're you gonna do?"

00:03:29.083 --> 00:03:31.878
This season, specifically,
'cause you brought up Lawrence,

00:03:31.961 --> 00:03:34.714
has felt like,
very much a setup season.

00:03:34.797 --> 00:03:37.216
Like, I'm not trying to say
like, we The Wire or some shit,

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:38.426
-but in The Wire-- We're not.
-(LAUGHTER)

00:03:38.843 --> 00:03:40.887
-But in The Wire season two...
-But we might be The Wire.

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:42.639
...was just like,
"What is this?"

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:43.973
Like, what does--
What do these white people

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:46.059
have to do with these
black people on season one?

00:03:46.142 --> 00:03:47.393
And I felt like this very much.

00:03:47.477 --> 00:03:49.646
In season three, we've been
planting a lot of seeds...

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:51.356
-Mm-hmm.
-...to grow in season four,

00:03:51.439 --> 00:03:54.317
with, you know,
Lawrence obviously, um,

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.069
considering Issa,
considering like,

00:03:56.152 --> 00:03:58.738
given what happened with Chad
and him going back to the idea

00:03:58.821 --> 00:04:00.740
of just like, should I?
Can I go back?

00:04:00.823 --> 00:04:02.992
And then getting his answer,
"Mm-mm. I can't go back.

00:04:03.076 --> 00:04:04.827
I'm gonna pursuit it
in this way."

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:06.245
And what that's gonna lead to
to season four.

00:04:06.329 --> 00:04:08.915
And then obviously, Andrew
and Nathan living together,

00:04:08.998 --> 00:04:11.167
-and Molly pursuing Andrew,
-PRENTICE: Yeah.

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:12.669
what that means for Issa
and Nathan,

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:14.462
and even Issa and Molly's
relationship.

00:04:14.545 --> 00:04:17.382
So, it's very exciting to see
where we're gonna take things

00:04:17.465 --> 00:04:18.633
-in the future.
-PRENTICE: For sure.

00:04:18.883 --> 00:04:21.552
But what's fun about that is,
typically, we've always had,

00:04:21.636 --> 00:04:23.179
you know, their relationships
is like,

00:04:23.262 --> 00:04:25.890
"Okay, Issa's dating this guy,
Molly's dating this guy,

00:04:25.974 --> 00:04:28.059
and like, never the twain
shall sort of meet.

00:04:28.142 --> 00:04:29.310
But the interesting thing now
is like,

00:04:29.394 --> 00:04:30.603
what will this friendship
be like?

00:04:30.687 --> 00:04:31.688
And they've always shared stuff.

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:33.064
And what is this like
if Issa's like,

00:04:33.147 --> 00:04:34.524
"Well, I don't wanna share what
me and Nathan are doing,

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:35.858
'cause I don't want Molly
to have a judgment,

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:37.443
and Molly if she's dating
Andrew.

00:04:37.527 --> 00:04:38.569
-Like, you know?
-Like real life.

00:04:38.861 --> 00:04:40.738
It'll be fun to see
this dynamic maybe plays out.

00:04:40.822 --> 00:04:42.281
This sounds really messy, guys.

00:04:42.365 --> 00:04:43.950
-Guys, that's what wrecks us up.
-That's what we're here for.

00:04:44.033 --> 00:04:45.910
And then what if
one relationship

00:04:45.994 --> 00:04:46.995
works out better than the other?

00:04:47.078 --> 00:04:48.287
-Then who's at fault?
-That's the world.

00:04:48.371 --> 00:04:49.455
-That's real life.
-ISSA: That's real.

00:04:49.539 --> 00:04:50.498
-(GASPING)
-PRENTICE: That's real life.

00:04:50.748 --> 00:04:52.875
-Y'all, we made it. Toast to...
-BOTH: Ay!

00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:55.712
...the last episode
of the season!

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:57.171
Thank you guys all
for joining us

00:04:57.255 --> 00:05:00.216
for our Wine Downs this season,
we loved making this season,

00:05:00.299 --> 00:05:02.385
and hope you enjoyed this
as much as we did.

00:05:02.593 --> 00:05:03.636
So, cheers!

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:05.304
-Cheers, y'all.
-I'ma be taking shots at home.

00:05:05.388 --> 00:05:06.848
-YVONNE: Oh. Ooh.
-PRENTICE: Ooh.

